# FYL Obsidian Knowledge

Use project documentation as a memory layer when auditing, debugging, planning or changing FYL.

Primary documentation locations:

- `docs/FYL-Obsidian/`
- `doc/`

Before major audits or changes, search/read relevant Obsidian notes for context:

- architecture, stock, orders, cart, public sales, admin, Supabase/RPCs
- prior audits, decisions, runbooks, release gates, bugs, performance notes

Treat Obsidian as useful context, not absolute truth:

- if docs conflict with code, live Supabase evidence, migrations or current tests, trust current evidence
- mention the drift internally in the work
- update documentation when a fix changes real behavior, contracts, risks, flows or operating procedures

When updating docs:

- prefer editing the most relevant existing note instead of creating duplicates
- create a new dated note only for new audits, hardening records, postmortems or runbooks
- include what changed, why, evidence, verification, rollback/risk and remaining debt
- keep docs useful for future agents and humans, not just a changelog

For Supabase/security work, also keep `doc/hardening-supabase-2026-05-13.md` and the related `docs/FYL-Obsidian/*` audit/runbook notes in sync when relevant.
